  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## 12.4.2\n\n### Fixes\n- `PdfFontEmbedding.Subset` embeds only the outlines of the glyphs the document uses. It behaved like `Full`, so every export carried whole font files. Glyph ids stay as they are, the unused outlines are left empty (TrueType `glyf` with composite parts kept, and CFF), and only the tables a viewer reads are kept, so the embedded program compresses to a fraction of the font. A font whose licence forbids subsetting, a CFF2 font and a font the subsetter cannot read safely are embedded whole. `Full` stays the default.\n- A paragraph's first-line indent moves its first line in the exported PDF, the same way the view lays it out, including a negative (hanging) indent. The PDF used an indent of 0. Like the view, this needs an Avalonia version whose text formatter applies `TextParagraphProperties.Indent` (AvaloniaUI/Avalonia#22870).",
